A grammatical illusion.

43:31.840 --> 43:35.800
And Flyxion took that simple observation, stripped it all the way down to the foundational

43:35.800 --> 43:41.280
mathematics of drawing a circle on a blank whiteboard, and then meticulously, relentlessly

43:41.280 --> 43:42.200
scaled it back up.

43:42.220 --> 43:43.120
Step by step.

43:43.260 --> 43:47.600
We went from a simple boundary to the physical energy costs required to maintain that boundary,

43:47.980 --> 43:52.760
to the mathematical blind spots it inevitably creates. We watched entropy erode those lines,

43:53.140 --> 43:57.680
we built repair mechanisms to fight the entropy, and we ultimately arrived at a universal geometric

43:57.680 --> 44:01.640
law for why entire civilizations or ecosystems survive or collapse.

44:01.640 --> 44:08.380
It is a totalizing synthesis. Flyxion is arguing that the universe is not a collection of static

44:08.380 --> 44:14.200
objects occasionally bumping into each other. It is a dynamic, desperate, ongoing ecology of

44:14.200 --> 44:18.800
boundaries, fighting to maintain their own capacity to keep drawing boundaries.

44:18.800 --> 44:22.460
It forces you to look at everything through a completely different lens.

44:22.760 --> 44:28.220
A highly successful company, a vibrant coral reef, a functioning democracy, none of these are things.

